    "prompt": "Single continuous take, one-shot, 12 seconds, 16:9, 24fps. NO cuts, NO transitions, NO scene changes — one uninterrupted camera movement from the first frame to the last.\nOpening frame:\n@image1 — the video starts exactly from @image1. Keep the woman, her outfit and shoes, the golf green, the golf club, lighting and color grading exactly as in @image1.\nPlastic head prop:\nUse @image2 as the identity reference for the head prop. The head placed on the tee must clearly look like the character from @image2 — same face, hairstyle and overall recognizable appearance — but it must be a plastic head, like a mannequin/display/toy head, not a real human head. It should have a rigid glossy plastic surface and clearly read as an artificial object.\nFinal character:\nThe character from @image2 — keep face, appearance and outfit exactly as in @image2, placed in the same location, lighting and color grading as @image1.\n[0s–2s] HEAD PLACEMENT\nExactly in the same top-down composition as @image1. At the start, the white tee near the golf club is empty. A hand of the woman from @image1 enters the frame naturally and places the small plastic head onto the white tee. The movement is elegant, deliberate and clearly readable. By 2s, the plastic head is fully resting on the tee, stable and centered.\n[2s–3s] STRIKE\nWithout any cut, still in the same top-down view, the woman swings the golf club and strikes the plastic head off the tee. Crisp, sharp impact. The strike is fully finished by 3s.\n[3s–8s] FLIGHT TO THE RIGHT\nWithout any cut, the plastic head is launched like a real golf ball and flies in one long high arc from left to right across the frame, spinning. The camera pans and travels to the right, following it.\n- 3s–4.5s: brief slow motion right after impact, the plastic head spins in close-up.\n- 4.5s: speed ramp back to real-time speed.\n- 4.5s–7s: real-time speed, the head flies fast along a high arc to the right, reaches the peak and starts falling, accelerating with real gravity.\n- 7s–8s: the plastic head drops fast and heavy like a real golf ball, straight down into an empty golf hole cup with a sharp hard hit — no floating, no slow gliding, no bouncing, no rolling — and disappears inside exactly at 8s. The camera arrives low at grass level, right above the hole.\n[8s–12s] REVEAL\nContinuing the same uninterrupted movement, the camera smoothly cranes up and tilts up from the hole. The hole stays in the foreground. In the background, about 15 meters behind the hole, beyond the edge of the golf green and outside the playing field, on a small raised grassy hill above the level of the hole, the character from @image2 is gradually revealed, seen from a slightly low angle, full figure by 10.5s. He stands in a posed fashion stance, body turned three-quarters to the camera (half-turned, not in profile), face turned toward the camera, running one hand through his hair to slick it back, the other hand in his trouser pocket, blank cold arrogant stare, lips closed, not smiling. 10.5s–12s: the camera holds steady on him against a clear blue sky.\nStyle:\nretro 70s–80s luxury fashion ad aesthetic, saturated colors, vivid green grass, clear blue sky, surreal playful humor, clean composition, realistic physics, realistic ball physics and gravity, realistic human motion. The plastic head and the final character are never shown transforming — the connection is implied only by the camera movement.\nAudio:\ngroovy vintage funk-lounge track with bass, subtle hand movement/placement sound at the beginning, club impact click at 2s, fast whoosh of flight, sharp hard clack as the plastic head drops into the cup at 8s."
