    "prompt": "Multi-shot sequence with hard cuts between shots. Keep the same main character, dog, wardrobe, and visual style throughout all shots.\n\nIMPORTANT CHARACTER REFERENCE:\n@image1 is the exact visual reference for the main character. Use the person from @image1 in every shot. Preserve their exact facial identity, facial structure, proportions, hairstyle, skin tone, age, and recognizable features throughout the entire sequence. Do not redesign, beautify, replace, or alter their face. The character must remain clearly recognizable as the person from @image1 in every shot.\n\nKeep the same wardrobe throughout: olive-green military jacket, khaki cargo pants and brown boots.\n\nDOG REFERENCE:\n@image2 is the exact visual reference for the dog. Use the dog from @image2 in every shot. Preserve its exact breed, size, coat color, coat length, and recognizable features. Maintain the same dog identity and proportions throughout the entire sequence.\n\nSHOT 1\nThe character from @image1, exhausted and covered in dirt, stands inside an abandoned ornate mansion, aiming a bolt-action rifle. Their face, identity and appearance must exactly match @image1. Sweat, dirt, a small cheek scrape and tears cover their face. Their hands tremble. They close their eyes as a tear rolls down their cheek, then hear something and slowly lower the rifle, visibly heartbroken.\n\nSHOT 2\nOver their shoulder, an infected version of the dog from @image2 sits on the debris-covered parquet floor. Matted fur, cloudy white eyes, wounds and dark veins. The dog trembles while softly whimpering and growling.\n\nSHOT 3\nThe character from @image1 slowly crouches, places the rifle on the floor, wipes their tears and gives the dog a small broken smile. They quietly speak to the dog, pull a worn yellow-green tennis ball from their jacket and gently roll it toward the dog.\n\nSHOT 4\nExtreme low-angle close-up of the tennis ball rolling through dust across the cracked parquet floor. It stops directly in front of the dog's paws. Hold on the still ball.\n\nHARD CUT / TRANSFORMATION\n\nSHOT 5\nSame low camera angle and exactly the same ball position, but now on a clean sunny residential basketball court. A healthy version of the dog from @image2 suddenly grabs the ball. Eyes clear and warm, fur clean, playful and energetic. The dog shakes and plays with the ball.\n\nSHOT 6\nWide shot of the basketball court. The character from @image1 throws the ball and the happy dog sprints after it, catches it, runs back and drops it at their feet, ready to play.\n\nSHOT 7\nClose-up of the character from @image1, now clean and unharmed, laughing while affectionately ruffling the dog's neck and chest. Their facial identity must remain exactly consistent with @image1. The dog happily pants beside them.\n\nSHOT 8\nWide peaceful shot. The character from @image1 and the dog sit together in a pristine dark-green vintage convertible beside the court. They share food from a tin can with the dog. The dog gently takes it and licks their fingers.\n\nCHARACTER CONSISTENCY\n\nMAIN CHARACTER:\nUse @image1 as the sole identity reference. Same person in every shot. Exact facial identity, structure, proportions, hairstyle and recognizable features from @image1. Natural skin texture. No face changes between shots. No different person. No facial morphing. No age changes. No beauty-filter effect. No exaggerated facial features.\n\nWARDROBE:\nOlive-green military jacket. Khaki cargo pants. Brown boots. Same clothing throughout the entire sequence.\n\nDOG:\nUse @image2 as the sole identity reference. Same dog throughout. Infected and injured in the mansion. Healthy, clean and playful after the transformation. Maintain the same recognizable dog identity and proportions from @image2.\n\nMANSION:\nAbandoned ornate interior, tall arched windows, torn dark-red curtains, peeling damask wallpaper, shattered gilt mirror, broken furniture, debris, ceiling hole and strong sunlight beams.\n\nCOURT:\nClean residential basketball court, white lines, iron fence, flowering shrubs, stone townhouses, warm late-afternoon sunlight and soft shadows. Dark-green vintage convertible with chrome trim.\n\nVISUAL STYLE:\nUltra-realistic, photorealistic, natural human and animal movement, handheld camera, shallow depth of field, ARRI Alexa 35 look, warm cinematic grade, subtle film grain, realistic skin texture, realistic lighting, cinematic composition.\n\nCAMERA:\nNatural handheld cinematography. Mix of wide shots, medium shots, over-the-shoulder shots, close-ups and extreme low-angle shots. Smooth but realistic camera movement. Maintain spatial continuity between shots.\n\nAUDIO:\nONLY natural diegetic sound. Natural breathing, house ambience, dog sounds, footsteps, clothing movement, tennis ball sounds, birds and wind. ABSOLUTELY NO MUSIC. ABSOLUTELY NO SCORE. ABSOLUTELY NO BACKGROUND MUSIC.\n\n"
